# The cross-module twin of `classes/pass_stub_abstract_members.spy`: `pass` is a co-equal stub body
# beside `...`/`(...)` for INTERFACE members (#1214), and one declaration must not classify two ways
# depending on which side of an import it sits (#1258). Value-returning `pass` stubs are rejected by
# must-return (SPY0266), so — like the same-file pin — the pinnable shape is None-returning.
#
# What this fixture pins is the END-TO-END behavior: a `pass`-bodied imported interface is
# implementable and callable through the interface. It does NOT pin
# ModuleLoader.ExtractFullInterfaceSymbol's classification, which was measured (2026-08-06, by
# disabling that marking outright) to be shadowed in every front end: since #1087 the entry file's
# local-import closure is lowered into a synthetic project and NameResolver resolves every unit, so
# the imported symbols come from NameResolver (#1267). `Semantic/StubClassificationTableTests` is
# the guard that fails when the two classifications disagree.
interface Logger:
    def log(self, message: str) -> None:
        pass

    def flush(self) -> None:
        pass
